From 9f89a2b449252604aade954d12c5fb24751025bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:57:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat(ops): pre-upgrade snapshot, restore script and
 image rollback tags

There was no backup or rollback path: upgrade.sh pulled, rebuilt and ran
'alembic upgrade head' with nothing to return to, and several Alembic
downgrades are incomplete.

- scripts/backup.sh: pg_dump (custom format) plus tar archives of the
  alpha_router_qdrant / alpha_router_seaweedfs / alpha_router_tls volumes,
  .env, docker-compose.override.yml and a MANIFEST (commit, image ids).
  --consistent stops qdrant/seaweedfs for the copy; keeps BACKUP_KEEP (7).
- scripts/restore.sh <snapshot> [--with-env] [--previous-images]: stops the
  stack (never down -v), pg_restore --clean, restores volumes, optionally
  re-tags <image>:prev -> :latest, starts the stack. Typed RESTORE confirmation.
- upgrade.sh: backup_before_upgrade (SKIP_BACKUP=1 to opt out) and
  tag_previous_images before 'compose up'.
- stack.sh: .env.bak.* copies get mode 600 and only the 5 newest are kept;
  .gitignore now covers .env.bak.* and .env.pre-restore.* (they hold every
  secret and were committable with 'git add -A').
- service detection captures 'compose ps' output before grep -q: under
  pipefail an early-closing grep could report a healthy service as not
  running (found by the harness; also fixed in deploy-mode.sh).
- scripts/tests/test-backup-flow.sh exercises the flow with a fake docker.
- README: backup / restore / rollback section.

